  v2: answered by PHREEQC (IPhreeqc, USGS) using wateq4f.dat plus USBM IC 9429 reference-temperature complexes, with the reviewed Sander HBr gas-uptake slice
    model:   WATEQ Debye-Hückel extension (reliable to about I = 1 mol/kgw)
    routing: the default inorganic aqueous dataset. some elements here keep the oxidation state they were added in: only the couples that equilibrate on a bench timescale exchange electrons, and the slow ones — sulfate, nitrate, carbonate — are held as added. The potential reported is the Cu/Cu+2 electrode's, by Nernst over the computed activity (3.879e-3; E° +0.3419 V, CRC) — a metal in contact with its ion sets the potential, not the air above the beaker. The speciation itself was solved at the open-air pe.
    the dataset records its own sources, e.g.:
      · WATEQ4F, Alpers and others, 1989
      · log K from llnl.dat  Aug 23, 2005
      · Dzombak and Morel, 1990
      · usbm-ic9429-complexes-25c
      · sander-2023-hbr-reference
